<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5178" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμεσος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>immediate:</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμεσα καὶ ἀναπόδεικτα,</span> of
			propositions <i>that cannot be proved syllogistically by means of a
				middle term,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>APr.</u>
				68b30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>APo.</u>
				72b19
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἄ. τῶν ἐναντίων</span>
			<i>direct</i> opposites, <i><span class="en">
				Plot.
				6.3.20
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμέσως</span>”
				<i>immediately,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Olymp.
					<u>in Phlb.</u>
					p.256
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				S.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.Aphr.
				<u>in Metaph.</u>
				162.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Procl.
				<u>Inst.</u>
				30
			</span></i>, dub. in <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Herc.</u>
				1251.3
			</span></i>. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμεσότης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τητος</span>, ἡ,
				<i>immediacy,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Eustr.
				<u>in APo.</u>
				176.4
			</span></i>. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμέσω:</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠμοπλάται,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> (cf. Lat. <i>umerus,</i> Goth. <i>ams-</i>).</div>
